From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:05:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the DSU PMU

The DynamIQ Shared Unit of the A733 has its own performance monitors
for the L3 cache, the snoop filter and the bus, which perf cannot use
without a node.

Add it for all eight cores of the one DSU cluster. The overflow
interrupt is nCLUSTERPMUIRQ, INTID 274 (SPI 242) in the user manual's
interrupt table. On the A733 the counters work and the interrupt fires
once per counter overflow.

The kernel runs at EL2, where the DSU PMU registers are only accessible
when the firmware has set ACTLR_EL3 bit 12 on every core. With firmware
that does not, the driver's first register access is an undefined
instruction, and the kernel cannot read the bit. Add the node disabled;
a board enables it together with firmware that sets the bit.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with the node enabled by
the board; arm_dsu_pmu probes arm_dsu_0 for cpus 0-7 on INTID 274
without an undefined instruction. No events were counted in this test.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 9cc778a2c00d..19d26bafbb32 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -293,6 +293,15 @@ l3_cache: l3-cache {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/* needs ACTLR_EL3 bit 12 from the boot firmware */
+	dsu_pmu: dsu-pmu {
+		compatible = "arm,dsu-pmu";
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 242 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+		cpus = <&cpu0>, <&cpu1>, <&cpu2>, <&cpu3>,
+		       <&cpu4>, <&cpu5>, <&cpu6>, <&cpu7>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	/* 19.2, 24 or 26 MHz, set by the board */
 	osc: osc-clk {
 		#clock-cells = <0>;
